WHY THIS RATHER THAN MIT

These documents exist to be quoted, cited, corrected and built on — by wikis
like The Cutting Room Floor and Data Crystal, by other researchers, and by
anyone writing about this game. CC BY is the licence those communities already
use and expect, and it asks for the one thing that actually matters here:
attribution, so a finding can be traced back to the work that produced it and
checked.

ATTRIBUTION

    Friday the 13th (NES) Technical Reference, by MLCJR
    https://github.com/  <repository URL>

WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER

  * Facts. This licence covers the expression — the writing, tables and
    diagrams — not the underlying facts about the game, which nobody owns and
    which you are free to restate however you like.
  * Quotations from the 1989 LJN instruction manual, the in-game text, and
    material attributed to The Cutting Room Floor, GameFAQs guide authors, or
    other named sources. Those belong to their respective rightsholders and are
    quoted here briefly for identification and commentary.
  * Section 16 of `README.md` is generated from
    a machine-checked manifest; the generator is MIT-licensed and lives in the
    project repository.

If in doubt about reusing something here, the answer is almost certainly yes —
credit MLCJR and go ahead.
